Falsifies `system_tests::user::net_confinement_tests::a_socket_holder_cannot_receive_on_its_socket_capability`,
its receive-probe assertion (`armed[2]`), added by risk 7's fifth outsider pass (2026-10-10 UTC).

Architecture: aarch64, riscv64, x86_64

The defect is the socket capability carrying `READ`. The stack mints each socket's capability from
`socket_contract::stack_slots::MINT`, a copy of its own serve endpoint. The mint is `WRITE | GRANT`
on purpose, with no `READ`, because a socket holder that could `RECEIVE` on its capability would
dequeue the stack's own incoming queue, every other client's request to the stack. This hunk gives
the mint `READ`, so the kernel's `RECEIVE` rights check (kernel/src/syscall.rs) passes and the
squatter's probe blocks on the stack's endpoint instead of being refused.

Expected to fail: the squatter's kernel `RECEIVE` on its own socket capability no longer returns
`NotPermitted`; it blocks on the stack's endpoint queue (no sender pending at that point), so the
squatter never sends its armed report and the test panics at `next_report(squatter, "squatter")`
rather than reaching `assert_eq!(armed[2], SQUATTER_RECV_REFUSED, ...)`. Confirmed red on
2026-10-10 (UTC) on aarch64 with `script/test --arch aarch64 --test a_squatter_at_a_shared_stack`:
`[PANIC] ... the squatter never reported: it, the stack or the peer is blocked`. The hunk is in
portable kernel wiring, so one patch serves every leg; riscv64 and x86_64 were not replayed by hand.

diff --git a/kernel/src/user/e1000e_service.rs b/kernel/src/user/e1000e_service.rs
index 13fa284d3..748ccdd2a 100644
--- a/kernel/src/user/e1000e_service.rs
+++ b/kernel/src/user/e1000e_service.rs
@@ -245,7 +245,7 @@ fn spawn_server(image: &'static [u8], listen_grant: u64, found: crate::e1000e::F
         // server's own address space, `run_with_own_space` adds once the space exists.
         at(
             socket_contract::stack_slots::MINT,
-            rendezvous_capability(stack, Rights::WRITE.union(Rights::GRANT)),
+            rendezvous_capability(stack, Rights::WRITE.union(Rights::GRANT).union(Rights::READ)),
         );
         run_with_own_space(
             image,
